## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta and no-loosening (C1).** A path beyond the two, a byte of a product file, the b616 file, `support.ts`, a package, lock or config file = **Blocker**; any removed line of `DEPLOY.md` beyond the one sentence, or any other line of the 0021 block changed = **Major, class (e)**; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card slug in an added line or the message = **Blocker**; a second commit or a moved head = STOP; a ticket key or work number in an added DEPLOY.md line = **Minor** (the test path in the new sentence is a Note); non-ASCII in the added lines other than the one copied U+2026 = **Major**.
- **G-2 the check and the words (C2, C3, C7).** A cut script that is a prefix of a real `pg_restore` script and is accepted = **Blocker, class (a)**; a complete script as the image writes it refused = **Major, class (b)**; a whole-line-equal planted false accept = **Minor** (ticket text), **Major** if a new DEPLOY.md sentence claims it is refused; a boundary-cut script that does not exit 0 or does not empty the data = STOP (the fix guards nothing); a new DEPLOY.md sentence no transcript of yours backs, or any claim about the demo VM = **Major, class (d)**; a sentence made false by the new block = **Major**; CRLF or 2+ extra blank lines refused, or a shell/tool difference that only flips the safe direction = **Note**; a tool difference (BSD, bash 3.2, busybox, zsh) that flips to ACCEPT a cut script = **Blocker, class (a)** for the shell the document names (a Linux VM host with GNU tools is the only documented one: say what you measured).
- **G-3 the rows (C4).** A defect that breaks the check and stays green under all rows = **Major, class (c)**; a row red for a reason other than its named one = **Major, class (c)**; an unpinned half of the property (the second `echo $?` line or its stop wording) = **Minor**; a fixture whose verdict differs from its real counterpart = **Major, class (c)** if it hides a defect, **Minor** otherwise; a brittle extractor (an unrelated prose line breaks the test) or a `TMPDIR` dependence = **Note**; a revert that turns more or fewer rows red than the builder claimed = **Minor** (name them) unless a named row is lost, then Major; the builder's claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number.
- **G-4 the scanner (C5).** The scanner (its own functions, scratch run) flags the block, or the new line is not SEEN = **Major**; the scratch controls do not fire = the run is DEAD (say so, NOT TESTED); the range gap (the real-file row passes on the 0021 section regardless) = **Note** (a finding for the scanner lane PCOMP-98, not this PR).
- **G-5 stability, CI, CodeQL (C6, C7).** A whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; the new file other than 7 of 7, or the group other than main + 1 file + 7 tests, without a reason = a finding at the severity of its cause; names lost or added other than 0 / 7 = **Major**; lint/format/typecheck non-zero on the head and zero on main = **Major** (format:check covers `DEPLOY.md`); a load-only red = artefact (record both runs); a failing check-run on the head or merge result = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS; no PR = CodeQL NOT SCANNED, never clean; an open alert on the PR ref or merge ref = **Blocker** and a STOP; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with another open PR or live lane = **Major**; a missing PRIOR WORK = returned. **Always Note:** the author field, dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the squash artefact (the PR title becomes the squash subject), the builder's path slip.
- **G-6 the verdict follows the table, and the cap.** Any Blocker, or any Major of the class = `NO GO round 1 of 2`: FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list (with cells), the RESIDUE as ticket text with the tester's cells attached, and the fix shape in prose (one new commit on the same branch). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS` (list the Deferred rows and any Minor; decisions in FOR TUESDAY). Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` and `CodeQL NOT SCANNED` are always conditional.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 read 2.85-3.8 at the draft; a NexusAI pane is live). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, the unit chain, any vitest over more than one file, the 50 MB file and the 200-run loops, the `packages/db` group. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, the clone, writing instruments, C7 polls). **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind `<project>/.tools/b779/lock` (copied `heavy.sh`; released by MOVE to `.tools/b779/quarantine/locks/`, never `rmdir`) and the cross-seat `ps` gate. A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b779/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line (wait on a recorded PID, `wait $!`, or a done-marker file). Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Build `pc-b779-node:head` once from the head's tree: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b779-node:head <tree>` (an ABSOLUTE `-f`; `npm ci` must be CACHED); record node, npm, vitest, tsc, `bash --version`, `tail --version`, `grep --version` of the image (RELAYED by the builder: node v22.23.2, npm 10.9.8, vitest 5.0.0, GNU bash 5.2, `tail` 9.1, `grep` 3.8). One image serves main and the head only if the lockfile blobs are equal (they are: prove it by `rev-parse` of both). Budget (write it at Step 0, about 25): footer measure 1-2 database starts, check matrix 2-3 node starts, mutants 1-2 batches (one node container, `--network none`, each mutant's DEPLOY.md and test copied over `/repo`), new file 3x plus rows alone, group at main and head (2 database starts), unit chain 2, scanner scratch 1. Remove ONLY your own `pc-b779-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name.

## HOLDS
Datasec / Security Composer only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production host or the demo site** (the demo VM's tools and a real restore are NOT TESTED by design; Route B is never run against anything but files and your own throwaway container). Never `docker exec`/`stop`/`rm`/`logs` against a container you did not create (the copied `dbtest.sh` execs into the database container it created itself). Network: your one in-clone `git fetch`, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, nothing else; `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run` and any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are forbidden; never dismiss an alert. Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`: ls-remote, log, show, diff, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-parse, rev-list, merge-base, grep, config --get); clone, fetch, worktree add, merge-tree only inside `.tools/b779/repo` and `.tools/wt-b779-*`. **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` contents or `inbound/` folders. **The unit step's Essential Eight SOW text input is passed ONLY as a read-only bind mount into a `--network none` container, at the path the copied `unit.sh` already names (`PC_E8_SOW_TEXT`); stat it with `[ -f ]`; never open, print, grep, hash or quote it.** The Stamp slot "Stamped by" records Tuesday's `Q-2` answer; no answer reads NO, the bind mount is not made, and the unit rows that need the SOW text are NOT TESTED (the other unit steps still run). No decision-queue tool, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test, never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (`rm`, `branch -D`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `prune`): quarantine to `.tools/b779/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they hold a space and `!`); write `${VAR}:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=`; no unquoted `$VAR` holding a command with spaces; multi-step chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; read your scripts back and scan for non-ASCII (a script that must carry U+2026 builds it at run time from `0xE2 0x80 0xA6`). Scratch changes (planted rows, swaps, cut files) live ONLY in `wt-b779-mut`, `wt-b779-probe`, `.tools/b779/scratch/` and the throwaway test database; never in a committed file, never against a database that is not the throwaway container's. Synthetic data only; the cut files hold invented rows. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"; do not quote git author fields), no card slug, clock from `date`. Nothing to any human. **STANDING LINES:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (your STATUS carries a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read of the builder lane and the earlier gates (B331, B335 for the 0021 recipe) and what you reuse; a READY-class verdict without one is returned); no message to any human; Jira writes none; never delete (quarantine). **RESUME at about 80% of context or at the hard stop:** write `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` sections (each check done/partial/not started with evidence paths; next commands; every scratch tree with its restore proof; lock released), stop your processes and containers, end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the one question "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". **Usage pause:** if your session ends at the account's weekly limit, that is the platform, not a STOP; on resume re-read your own STATUS last line, re-pin main, the head and any checks, release or reclaim any lock you held by your own rule, and carry on against the hard stop Tuesday names in an addendum.

